  Exercise 26.1 - Distributed Training: Scaling Analysis
======================================================================

-- Section 1: Ring AllReduce Cost --

  Ring AllReduce of S bytes across N GPUs moves ~2(N-1)/N * S bytes per GPU,
  so time ~= 2(N-1)/N * S / B for interconnect bandwidth B.

  NVLink ~600 GB/s       7B bf16 grads, 8 GPUs:      40.8 ms / step
  InfiniBand ~50 GB/s    7B bf16 grads, 8 GPUs:     490.0 ms / step
  [check] AllReduce cost scales inversely with interconnect bandwidth

-- Section 2: ZeRO Per-GPU Memory --

  Adam training state per parameter (mixed precision, rough): ~2 bytes weights
  + ~2 grads + ~12 optimizer (fp32 master + m + v) = ~16 bytes/param.
  DDP replicates all of it; ZeRO shards progressively across N GPUs.

  ddp    (7B, 8 GPUs):   112.0 GB / GPU
  zero1  (7B, 8 GPUs):    38.5 GB / GPU
  zero2  (7B, 8 GPUs):    26.2 GB / GPU
  zero3  (7B, 8 GPUs):    14.0 GB / GPU
  [check] memory falls monotonically DDP -> ZeRO-1 -> 2 -> 3

-- Section 3: Scaling Efficiency --

  Efficiency = (speedup on N GPUs) / N. 1.0 is perfect; keep it >= 0.8.

  measured throughput: {1: 100, 2: 190, 4: 360, 8: 640}
  efficiency:          {1: 1.0, 2: 0.95, 4: 0.9, 8: 0.8}
  Amdahl ceiling @5% serial, 8 GPUs: 5.93x
  [check] efficiency computed; 8-GPU efficiency >= 0.80

